{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1336326","title":"Developing and Benchmarking One Health Genomic Surveillance  Tools for Influenza A Virus in Wastewater","description":"We benchmarked four targeted enrichment methods suited for sequencing-based surveillance of Influenza A Virus in wastewater: 1) a custom probe-capture enrichment panel, 2) a custom tiled-amplicon panel for the HA segment, 3) the Twist Comprehensive Viral Research probe-capture panel, 4) the universal amplicon method developed by Zhou et al 2009. We tested these 4 methods a) on direct mixtures of wastewater RNA and RNA from 4 strains of Influenza A virus, and b) on incubated mixtures of Influenza A Viruses spiked into wastewater and concentrated by either Promega Wizard Enviro TNA kit or Innovaprep CP Select + Qiagen AllPrep PowerViral extraction kit.","center":"University of California, Berkeley","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2025/09/29 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN52066602","Direct mixture of wastewater RNA and RNA from 4 Influenza A Virus strains, low concentration","uncertain",null,"2024-10-08",2024,"US","California",null,null,"unresolved",null,null,"USA: California",null,null,null,"Wastewater [ENVO:00002001]","environmental sample; urban association not established"],["SAMN52066603","Direct mixture of wastewater RNA and RNA from 4 Influenza A Virus strains, medium concentration","uncertain",null,"2024-10-08",2024,"US","California",null,null,"unresolved",null,null,"USA: California",null,null,null,"Wastewater [ENVO:00002001]","environmental sample; urban association not established"],["SAMN52066604","Direct mixture of wastewater RNA and RNA from 4 Influenza A Virus strains, high concentration","uncertain",null,"2024-10-08",202